      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 294.28,
      "end_seconds": 308.97,
      "duration_seconds": 14.69,
      "text": "I can't promise yet but most people with possible carbon monoxide poisoning do well once it's treated properly. Just to be sure I understood. You've had a headache mild and no chest pain or rash."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 314.47,
      "end_seconds": 316.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.12,
      "text": "That's it it yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 317.14,
      "end_seconds": 322.09,
      "duration_seconds": 4.95,
      "text": "Let's get a carboxyhaemoglobin blood test, for possible carbon monoxide poisoning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 324.1,
      "end_seconds": 325.7,
      "duration_seconds": 1.6,
      "text": "does it hurt?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 327.73,
      "end_seconds": 354.33,
      "duration_seconds": 26.6,
      "text": "I'll start you on high-flow oxygen, 15 litres per minute, continuous, until reviewed that's for carbon monoxide poisoning the pharmacy will go through the details again when you pick it it up leave the house now, don't use the boiler, and call the gas emergency number do get help quickly if the symptoms get worse we'll catch up straight away have I covered everything you wanted?"
    },
